{
  "_comment": "OPT-IN, OFF BY DEFAULT. Copy to hooks/hooks.json to enable. This GATES risky tool use: before a matching Bash command runs, it audits the current repo with the deterministic skillsentry CLI; on a BLOCK verdict the CLI exits non-zero and the hook BLOCKS the tool call, surfacing the reason on stderr (output is NOT swallowed — a BLOCK must be visible). Trade-off: it re-scans the repo per matching call, so the matcher is scoped to git/curl/install-shaped commands rather than every Bash; widen or narrow `matcher` to taste. The CLI never executes audited content, so this is safe — but turning it on is your explicit choice.",
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Bash(git:*)",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/cli/bin.js\" . --ci 1>&2"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
